Vendored components
===================

The following files in this directory are copied verbatim from
dhjoo98/mustafar (https://github.com/dhjoo98/mustafar), which is itself
derived from Flash-LLM (https://github.com/flash-llm/flash-llm). Both are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The original copyright and
license headers are retained in each file.

  AsyncCopy_PTX.cuh       - cp.async / ldmatrix helpers
  MMA_PTX.cuh             - mma.m16n8k16 FP16 / FP32-accumulate wrappers
  MatMulUtilities.cuh     - PipelinedCoreComputations, tile copy / store
  Reduction_Kernel.cuh    - split-K reduction
  TilingConfig.h          - Flash-LLM tiling constants

Those files are kept for reference and for the primitives that are reused
directly. Of the five, only MMA_PTX.cuh is `#include`d by a translation unit
that gets compiled: sparse_kernel.cu includes it, alongside
`../packed_abi.cuh` (which is ours). Nothing includes the other four.

The purpose-built code in this directory (sparse_kernel.cu,
bindings.cpp) is original to mustafar and targets the 328-byte TopMag50
packed layout. It reuses dhjoo98/mustafar's MSB-first bitmap scan
convention and its mma.m16n8k16 FP16 / FP32-accumulate wrapper; the
tiling, the K_Global-dependent word indexing and the per-tile `idx`
offset table of the Flash-LLM SpMM kernels are not used, because those
are tied to a 4096-wide contraction that this workload does not have.

